    <!-- Effects group: svgrepo.com/svg/525418/magic-stick-3 (Isaiah's pick), redrawn as
         STROKE work on the house 24-unit grid. Why, and the rule it is following:

         Survey's own Shapes glyph carries the law in its file header — a top-toolbar glyph
         should paint about the ink its neighbours do, and Survey's owner rejected their
         previous Shapes artwork for exactly this reason ("the filled version painted ~2x
         the ink of its top-toolbar neighbours ... it read bigger AND heavier than
         everything beside it"). WinShot had shipped the identical mistake here: the
         svgrepo source is five SOLID fills, so Effects was the only filled glyph in a row
         of outlines. Measured at 18 px it painted 78.6 px2 of ink against a top-row band of
         50-66, and the three solid sparkles collapsed into noise below 20 px — on a 150 %
         screen the button read as a grey smudge rather than a wand.

         Same composition, same reading: head at the top-left, shaft running to the
         bottom-right tip, three sparkles at the same three positions. Stroke 1.8 on the
         24-grid is 1.35 px at the 18 px host — inside the 1.25 (Pan) to 1.60 (Select) band
         its neighbours occupy. The sparkles are crossed strokes rather than solid stars
         because a filled 4-point star under 3 units across is a dot at this size; lucide's
         own wand-sparkles makes the same call. -->
    <Viewbox x:Key="SurveyIcon.Effects" x:Shared="False" Width="18" Height="18">
        <Canvas Width="24" Height="24">
            <!-- The wand: one outlined taper from the head cap to the tip, 3.0 half-width at
                 the head and 1.9 at the tip, both ends capped on their own centre. -->
            <Path Style="{StaticResource SurveyIconStroke}"
                  Data="M3.48,7.72 A3,3 0 0 1 7.72,3.48 L20.94,18.26 A1.9,1.9 0 0 1 18.26,20.94 Z"/>
            <!-- Where the head meets the shaft; the taper's own width at that point. -->
            <Path Style="{StaticResource SurveyIconStroke}"
                  Data="M7.28,11.12 L11.12,7.28"/>
            <!-- Sparkles: big, medium, small, at the source artwork's three positions. -->
            <Path Style="{StaticResource SurveyIconStroke}"
                  Data="M16.5,2.3 V6.7 M14.3,4.5 H18.7"/>
            <Path Style="{StaticResource SurveyIconStroke}"
                  Data="M20.6,8.8 V12 M19,10.4 H22.2"/>
            <Path Style="{StaticResource SurveyIconStroke}"
                  Data="M5.6,15.2 V18.4 M4,16.8 H7.2"/>
        </Canvas>
    </Viewbox>

    <!-- The REDACT tool's glyph, and the only thing that renders it. It used to be a Segoe
         MDL2 code point (&#xE7E6;) set as a ToggleButton's text Content, and StripToolButton
         never sets FontFamily — so the code point fell back to the UI font and the button
         rendered a literal tofu box. Every icon in this toolbar is a path now.

         Survey has no region-redaction glyph to port: its Blur and Pixelate tools do not
         exist any more (they are two of the four STYLES of WinShot's re-editable redaction
         mark), and its text-redact.svg is an "A under a black bar" for redacting selected
         TEXT — the wrong idea for a dragged region. So this is WinShot's own mark, drawn to
         the house rules, using the mosaic that was already in this file.

         Rebalanced from the old 9-cell grid, which measured 113.8 px2 of ink at 18 px —
         roughly double the 50-66 band its neighbours occupy, because it carried four solid
         5-unit cells AND five stroked ones. A five-cell checkerboard says "pixelated" with
         the ink of one glyph instead of two, and the empty cells do the same work the
         stroked ones did without paying for them. -->
    <Viewbox x:Key="SurveyIcon.Pixelate" x:Shared="False" Width="18" Height="18">
        <Canvas Width="24" Height="24">
            <Rectangle Style="{StaticResource SurveyIconFill}" Canvas.Left="3.2"  Canvas.Top="3.2"  Width="4.6" Height="4.6"/>
            <Rectangle Style="{StaticResource SurveyIconFill}" Canvas.Left="16.2" Canvas.Top="3.2"  Width="4.6" Height="4.6"/>
            <Rectangle Style="{StaticResource SurveyIconFill}" Canvas.Left="9.7"  Canvas.Top="9.7"  Width="4.6" Height="4.6"/>
            <Rectangle Style="{StaticResource SurveyIconFill}" Canvas.Left="3.2"  Canvas.Top="16.2" Width="4.6" Height="4.6"/>
            <Rectangle Style="{StaticResource SurveyIconFill}" Canvas.Left="16.2" Canvas.Top="16.2" Width="4.6" Height="4.6"/>
        </Canvas>
    </Viewbox>

